WEBVTT

NOTE Captions of the mcp-audit explainer (v3), from its narration.

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.223
Audits rarely fail for lack of automation.

2
00:00:03.243 --> 00:00:07.665
They suffer when auditors drown in
documents, spreadsheets and follow-ups.

3
00:00:07.685 --> 00:00:10.462
mcp-audit is built on one idea:

4
00:00:10.482 --> 00:00:13.785
AI does the groundwork, and the auditor
makes the calls.

5
00:00:14.505 --> 00:00:16.339
Three rules hold everywhere.

6
00:00:16.359 --> 00:00:20.503
AI only proposes: you accept, edit or
reject.

7
00:00:20.523 --> 00:00:24.415
Every change is versioned, showing who
made it, and on whose behalf.

8
00:00:24.435 --> 00:00:27.492
And missing evidence means no reasonable
assurance,

9
00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:29.483
never an invented non-conformity.

10
00:00:30.203 --> 00:00:30.855
You choose how AI takes part: the AI
buttons built into the app;

11
00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:31.475
your own assistant, such as Claude,
ChatGPT or Claude Code,

12
00:00:31.495 --> 00:00:32.105
connected through MCP under the same
rules; or no AI at all.

13
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:42.530
Models run through a gateway:

14
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:45.758
Claude, another provider, or a local
model,

15
00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:49.137
so documents never leave your
infrastructure.

16
00:00:49.157 --> 00:00:52.881
Self-host it as one container, or use a
hosted instance.

17
00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.101
It starts with the library.

18
00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.387
Import a law or standard.

19
00:00:57.407 --> 00:01:01.739
AI finds whom it applies to, such as
essential and important entities,

20
00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:06.339
and extracts only auditable requirements,
each worded to stand on its own.

21
00:01:07.059 --> 00:01:08.900
Then the audit runs in five steps,

22
00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.911
and the built-in guide shows what to do on
each screen.

23
00:01:11.931 --> 00:01:13.616
Step one: set up.

24
00:01:13.636 --> 00:01:17.167
Pick the auditee's role, and only its
requirements are offered.

25
00:01:17.187 --> 00:01:20.495
Choose the scopes, and one finding or one
per scope.

26
00:01:20.515 --> 00:01:23.552
AI derives the auditee's roles from their
documents,

27
00:01:23.572 --> 00:01:25.316
and risks from their register.

28
00:01:25.336 --> 00:01:26.687
You decide what stays.

29
00:01:27.407 --> 00:01:29.624
Step two: the auditee's own rules.

30
00:01:29.644 --> 00:01:32.050
Upload their policies and procedures.

31
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:36.715
AI extracts internal requirements, each
with an exact quote, its section,

32
00:01:36.735 --> 00:01:38.888
and the requirement it implements.

33
00:01:38.908 --> 00:01:41.979
When a new version arrives, every rule is
rechecked.

34
00:01:42.699 --> 00:01:43.984
Step three: plan.

35
00:01:44.004 --> 00:01:46.950
Enter the fieldwork days, hours and
exceptions.

36
00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:50.749
AI drafts the meetings, and the evidence
to collect at each.

37
00:01:50.769 --> 00:01:53.685
Coverage shows any requirement not yet
planned.

38
00:01:53.705 --> 00:01:56.972
You export the plan, and only you mark it
sent and agreed.

39
00:01:57.692 --> 00:01:59.873
Step four: run, on your phone.

40
00:01:59.893 --> 00:02:01.416
Take notes as you go:

41
00:02:01.436 --> 00:02:05.865
/ for a promise or a suspected issue, @ to
mention a requirement.

42
00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:08.419
Meeting transcripts land in the inbox.

43
00:02:08.439 --> 00:02:11.059
AI links the material to the planned
evidence,

44
00:02:11.079 --> 00:02:13.011
and you send the follow-up report.

45
00:02:13.731 --> 00:02:15.287
Step five: conclude.

46
00:02:15.307 --> 00:02:18.926
For every requirement and scope, AI
proposes a finding,

47
00:02:18.946 --> 00:02:21.374
with a rationale citing the evidence.

48
00:02:21.394 --> 00:02:24.538
While evidence is missing, or an issue is
open,

49
00:02:24.558 --> 00:02:27.567
the honest answer is no reasonable
assurance.

50
00:02:27.587 --> 00:02:31.311
Only you approve, and the report holds
approved findings only.

51
00:02:32.031 --> 00:02:34.676
From your own assistant, it is a
conversation.

52
00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:36.464
Ask what is missing next.

53
00:02:36.484 --> 00:02:40.254
Claude reads the engagement through MCP,
drafts proposals,

54
00:02:40.274 --> 00:02:43.979
and every change is recorded as Claude, on
behalf of you.

55
00:02:44.699 --> 00:02:46.907
More time for interviews and judgement.

56
00:02:46.927 --> 00:02:48.535
Consistent coverage.

57
00:02:48.555 --> 00:02:51.368
A full audit trail behind every
conclusion.

58
00:02:51.388 --> 00:02:53.098
Not an automated auditor.

59
00:02:53.118 --> 00:02:54.341
A better-equipped one.
